  "_about": "a scarlet ibis wading: brilliant scarlet all over, the wingtips black; the long down-curved bill, reddish and darker toward the tip; long scarlet legs; it flies with the neck stretched out and the legs trailing (2026-11-08, tools/creaturegen/sweep/necks.py) The NECK is one `sweep` (sculpt.js) along the chain of neck bones, not a tube a bone blended into the next: no bead at the joints. (2026-11-08, tools/creaturegen/sweep/flynecks.py) ALOFT the neck is held nearly straight ahead with a slight sag: the neck sweep is skinned from the body along its bones with its hand-offs on the rest curve's bends (`knotsAt`, `spread`), and the neck bones' and head's `flyRot` set with them.",
